    warnings: ['Human review is mandatory for symptom-only, detached, upper-surface-only, mixed-pathogen, culture-unlinked, ITS-only, single-locus-only, low-resolution, generated, stock, or rights-unclear samples.', 'Round pale-centered lesions, dark borders, yellow halos, chlorosis, center loss, defoliation, and lower-canopy onset are not unique to Cercospora.', 'The cf. flagellaris designation is laboratory-bounded and cannot be resolved from lesion color, lesion dimensions, central dark structures, one culture, or ordinary image and video evidence.', 'The two-to-six-millimeter lesion range, Florida foliage involvement, Kentucky canopy patterns, and seven- or fourteen-day controlled results are study-specific observations, not universal timing, severity, cultivar, yield, or action thresholds.', 'Cercospora, Bipolaris, and Septoria occurred together in Kentucky field experiments; a combined leaf-spot severity or yield result cannot be assigned to Cercospora alone.', 'The UF/IFAS Figure 3 composite is an attributed institutional differential, not a lesion-linked laboratory record; its CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 license prohibits derivatives and commercial reuse without additional permission.', 'A positive organism result from one sampled lesion does not establish that every lesion on a plant or in a field has the same cause.'],
